      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a steamboat‑building hub before becoming known for oil and casket production in the 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Captain William Vicary House, a stone mansion built by the town’s namesake, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
